I reported about this before for 1.5: there is a problem with sysinst
switching the terminal to cooked mode. I noticed it several times before
on the VAX, because it is a testing machine, but now I also noticed when
I upgraded my Alpha to 1.6. See below for the original message.

Also, sysinst cannot be used on an Adm-12 terminal. The Enter key is
interpreted the same as the Cursor Down key, so it is impossible to make
any menu selection. (the cursor down key generates ^J and enter
generates ^M). I had to plug in another terminal for installation.

